<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abel Aubert du Petit-Thouars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1793">1793</a>–<a href="/years/1864">1864</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abel Aubert du Petit-Thouars was a French naval officer who extended French power in the Pacific. In 1842 he took possession of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marquesas-islands">Marquesas Islands</a> and imposed a French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> on Tahiti under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomare-iv">Queen Pōmare</a> IV, and in 1843 he declared Tahiti annexed, a step disavowed by the French government. The resistance that followed led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franco-tahitian-war">Franco-Tahitian War</a> of 1844–1847.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abel-aubert-du-petit-thouars.jpg" alt="Abel Aubert du Petit-Thouars" width="170" height="274" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DupetitThouarsAA.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
